# A push in a loop under a trial visit counts as a write to its receiver alone only if that receiver is an array that is allocated here and that the loop's source only fills.
# What is known about every other object then survives the loop header.
# Here the array that is pushed to is the array that is read, and its length is the loop's bound.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeLocalArrayReceivers: every receiver is treated that way and is recorded among no objects that are written,
# so the length from before the loop is remembered all the way around it. The loop silently runs three iterations instead of three hundred.
# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime the remembered length is checked against memory.
